  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "AI Notepad",
      "text": "[English](README.md) | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\n[](https://github.com/JackWangSIA/dsh-ai-notepad/actions/workflows/ci.yml)\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <img src=\"assets/icon-180.png\" width=\"112\" alt=\"AI Notepad\">\n</p>\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <strong>A lightweight, general-purpose, AI-native text editor for DeepSeek Harness.</strong><br>\n  Plain text editing + selection-scoped AI + Windows file associations.\n</p>"
    },
    {
      "section": "AI Notepad",
      "text": "AI Notepad is a DeepSeek Harness plugin that turns the Harness Web UI into a lightweight, general-purpose AI text editor."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "From the plugin market after the listing is live. The market entry uses the\nversion-free GitHub Release tarball, so no npm account is required.\n\nFrom GitHub:\n\n```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web add JackWangSIA/dsh-ai-notepad\n```\n\nA prebuilt tarball is available at:\n\n```text\nhttps://github.com/JackWangSIA/dsh-ai-notepad/releases/latest/download/dsh-ai-notepad.tgz\n```\n\nIf the package is later published to npm, `dsh plugin --profile web add dsh-ai-notepad`\nwill also work."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "On DSH Desktop, prefer **Plugins → Add plugin** with the repository URL. The `desktop` profile is managed by the app; do not edit it with the CLI by hand."
    },
    {
      "section": "What works",
      "text": "- Open, edit, save and Save As any text file through a native Windows picker, or drop a file onto the editor.\n- Multi-tab editing with CodeMirror 6, undo/redo, find, line numbers, wrapping, and unsaved-change prompting.\n- Encoding-aware I/O: UTF-8, UTF-8 BOM, UTF-16 LE/BE, GB18030/GBK and Windows-1252. Saves preserve the detected encoding, BOM and dominant line ending. GB18030/Windows-1252 round-trip checks refuse lossy writes.\n- Binary-file detection protects files from accidental text editing.\n- Hash-based compare-before-write: if another program changed the file while it was open, the save returns a conflict and does not write.\n- Selection-scoped AI editing: concise, polish, expand, restructure, proofread, or a custom instruction.\n- Whole-document AI: polish, concise, summarize, outline and title generation.\n- A diff review modal with accept, reject and regenerate. Nothing is written before acceptance. Accepting uses a normal CodeMirror transaction, so Ctrl+Z still works.\n- Multiple annotations can be collected and sent in one batch; every reviewed region is validated against the original document before a single undoable edit.\n- Markdown preview with escaped raw HTML and a cons"
    },
    {
      "section": "Shortcuts",
      "text": "| Shortcut | Action |\n|---|---|\n| `Ctrl+S` / `Ctrl+Shift+S` | Save / Save As |\n| `Ctrl+Z` / `Ctrl+Y` | Undo / Redo |\n| `Ctrl+F` | Find |\n| `Ctrl+E` | Toggle Markdown preview / edit |\n| `Ctrl+wheel`, `Ctrl+=`, `Ctrl+-`, `Ctrl+0` | Font zoom in / out / reset |\n| `Ctrl+Alt+1..4` | Selection concise / polish / expand / proofread |\n| `Ctrl+Alt+B` | Add annotation |\n| `Ctrl+Alt+N` | Focus AI Notepad from the main shell |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Important Windows limitation",
      "text": "Windows 10/11 protects the default-app choice with a per-user `UserChoice` hash. No third-party application can silently force itself to become the default. AI Notepad therefore registers a real current-user `OpenWithProgids` entry, after which the user chooses it once in Explorer's **Open with → Always use this app**. The plugin can open Windows Default Apps for that choice, but it does not fake the system default. Uninstalling removes the ProgID and Open With entries; if AI Notepad is the current `UserChoice`, it removes that choice so Windows asks again. It cannot restore a previous hash-protected default."
    },
    {
      "section": "Important Windows limitation",
      "text": "The desktop shell has a single-instance lock but currently ignores file paths in its argv. The VBS launcher is therefore not a simulation: it is the registered file handler, and it delivers paths to the running Harness through the plugin inbox. A second launch focuses the existing window."
    },
    {
      "section": "Architecture",
      "text": "- `lib/index.js` — Host half. Connection `/api/ai-notepad/*` routes, bounded file I/O, encoding, conflict guards, LLM calls, Windows registry, inbox watcher, pickers, font enumeration.\n- `src/` — Client source. `app.jsx` is the full main-column page, `editor.jsx` owns CodeMirror, `store.js` owns tabs/AI/review/settings, `diff.js` and `markdown.js` are pure helpers.\n- `lib/client.js` — generated classic ModuleLoader bundle (React and `react/jsx-runtime` stay external).\n- `lib/scripts/` — native file pickers, font enumeration and the Windows external-open launcher.\n- `scripts/build.mjs` — esbuild bundle step.\n- `test/` — Host route/integration tests, encoding tests, VBS→inbox test, store AI/batch tests, ModuleLoader load test, and server-render tests for app/review/preview."
    },
    {
      "section": "Build and install",
      "text": "```powershell\n$node = \"$env:USERPROFILE\\.dsh\\dsh-runtimes\\dsh-primary-runtime\\dependencies\\node\\bin\\node.exe\"\n$pnpm = \"$env:USERPROFILE\\.dsh\\dsh-runtimes\\dsh-primary-runtime\\dependencies\\pnpm\\bin\\pnpm.mjs\"\n& $node $pnpm install --ignore-scripts --dir .\n& $node scripts/build.mjs\n\nThen install the absolute directory with the Harness `plugin_manager` `install_bundle` action. Do not copy files into the profile manually."
    },
    {
      "section": "Verification notes",
      "text": "The plugin installs and its Host row is active; the Client registers a main page, a sidebar panel icon and a settings section. Automated tests cover file I/O, encoding, conflict handling, AI request/response shapes with a fake LLM, selection/batch review and apply, generated client load, VBS queue delivery, and server-side rendering of the app, review and preview views. Live behavior was exercised through Windows UI Automation; screenshots in `assets/` come from the running desktop app."
    },
